463 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Vineyard City achieved a significant milestone by expanding its roadway connectivity and adding new roads and extensions to its existing network. This strategic UDOT and Vineyard City effort, coupled with the maintenance and extension of sidewalks and recreational trails, reflects a commitment to enhancing vehicular and pedestrian infrastructure. The FrontRunner Station, a key element of the city's transportation network, has been seamlessly integrated, contributing to a more efficient transit system. Opening the 1600 North Road connection from Lindon Marina to Geneva Road provides residents with direct access to Vineyard City from the 1600 North corridor, further enhancing accessibility and connectivity. Vineyard City's forward-thinking urban planning is evident in this comprehensive approach, laying the foundation for sustainable growth, improved accessibility, and an enhanced quality of life for its residents. This milestone represents a pivotal moment in the city's development, fostering a more connected and vibrant community.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
