/ActualText (When a few ancient trees in Gammon Park were taken down recently, for safety concerns, Mayor Fullmer reached out and helped city staff organize a service project. The old trees were bucked and delivered from the city, to Chief Executive Mary Meyer of the Timpanogos Nation. City staff were honored to have a chance to hear Chief Meyer's relay a few stories of past generations of her people, while visiting with her while dropping off the much appreciated firewood.)
